status_prefab_editor_create_part = Create a new logical part from the selected Geometry Objects. The objects move into the part rather than being duplicated. Parts let a section of the Prefab have its own name, parent, pivot, motion, and behavior in every linked instance.
status_prefab_editor_set_pivot = Set the selected part's pivot to the center of the currently selected vertices, faces, or objects. Swinging parts rotate around this point; for a door, select geometry along the hinge edge first.
status_prefab_editor_remove_part = Remove the selected logical part without deleting its Geometry Objects. Its objects are reassigned to another remaining part, while support surfaces and behavior attached specifically to the removed part are deleted. A Prefab must keep at least one part.
status_prefab_editor_prefab_name = Rename the reusable Prefab asset. Its UUID, linked instances, paint, geometry, and authored behavior remain unchanged; every linked instance will show the new name.
status_prefab_editor_part_name = Rename the selected logical part. This changes its authoring label only; the part's stable identity, geometry assignment, hierarchy, and linked instances are preserved.
status_prefab_editor_part_parent = Choose which part owns this part in the hierarchy. Child parts follow their parent's transformation and motion. Choose No Parent to make it a root-level part; cyclic parenting is prevented.
status_prefab_editor_part_assignment = Assign the currently selected Geometry Objects to this part. The geometry is moved between logical parts, not copied, so it will use the chosen part's pivot, hierarchy, and behavior.
status_prefab_editor_part_pivot = The stored pivot of the selected part in Prefab-local coordinates. Use Set Pivot after selecting vertices, faces, or objects to change it.
status_prefab_editor_door_angle = Set the signed swing angle in degrees. Positive and negative values open in opposite directions; valid values are -180 through 180, excluding zero. This value is ignored for sliding doors.
status_prefab_editor_door_layout = Choose Single for one moving door part. Choose Split for two fitted leaves; select the two leaf objects before using Make Door / Gate so Eldiron can assign and animate both sides.
status_prefab_editor_door_motion = Choose Swing to rotate around each part's pivot, or Slide to translate along the fitted motion axis. Set the pivot carefully for swinging doors.
status_prefab_editor_door_slide_distance = Set how far a sliding door travels in Prefab-local units. This is used only when Motion is Slide; fitted geometry may supply a sensible initial distance.
status_prefab_editor_door_usage_distance = Maximum horizontal distance from which the player may use this door or gate. A smaller value requires the player to stand closer to the Prefab.
status_prefab_editor_configure_door = Turn the selected fitted geometry into an interactive Door / Gate using the Leaves, Motion, angle, distance, and usage settings below. Interaction applies to the complete moving part, and the closed authored geometry is preserved.
status_prefab_editor_preview_door = Toggle a non-destructive preview between the authored closed state and the configured open state. The preview does not change the Prefab and closes automatically when you resume geometry editing.
status_prefab_editor_create_support_surface = Create an item-placement surface from the selected coplanar faces. The faces must belong to one Prefab part; their geometry is referenced, not duplicated or modified.
status_prefab_editor_edit_support_surface = Open settings for the surface selected in the hierarchy. Configure its name, placement grid, accepted item tags, capacity, and overlap policy without changing its geometry.
status_prefab_editor_remove_support_surface = Remove the selected placement definition and its item-placement behavior. The Geometry faces used by the surface are not deleted or modified.
status_prefab_editor_surface_name = Name this placement surface so it can be identified in the Prefab hierarchy and later by authoring or scripting tools. Renaming does not change its referenced faces.
status_prefab_editor_surface_snap = Grid spacing for item placement in Prefab-local units. Use 0 for continuous free placement; larger values snap placed items to evenly spaced positions on the surface.
status_prefab_editor_surface_tags = Comma-separated item tags accepted by this surface. Leave empty to accept any item; otherwise an item must match an allowed tag before it can be placed here.
status_prefab_editor_surface_capacity = Maximum number of items that may occupy this surface. Leave empty for no explicit limit; the overlap policy can still reject a position.
status_prefab_editor_surface_policy = Control spatial occupancy: Reject Overlap blocks intersecting placements, Allow Overlap permits them, and Single Occupant allows only one item on the entire surface.
status_prefab_surface_select_faces = Select one or more faces before creating a placement surface.
